le of the camera, measured in degrees. A value of","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"0"},{"text":" results in a camera pointed straight down at the map. Angles greater","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"than ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"0"},{"text":" result in a camera angled toward the horizon.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"name":"pitch"},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The camera’s heading, measured in degrees clockwise from true","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"north. A value of ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"0"},{"text":" means that the top edge of the map view corresponds to","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"true north. The value ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"90"},{"text":" means the top of the map is pointing due east.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"The value ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"180"},{"text":" means the top of the map points due south, and so on.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"name":"heading"}],"kind":"parameters"},{"kind":"content","content":[{"level":2,"text":"Discussion","anchor":"discussion","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"This method interprets the distance as a straight-line distance from the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"viewpoint to the center coordinate. To specify the altitude of the viewpoint,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"use the ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/org.swift.MyProject\/documentation\/MapLibre\/MLNMapCamera\/cameraLookingAtCenterCoordinate:altitude:pitch:heading:","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" method.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"sections":[],"kind":"symbol","identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/org.swift.MyProject\/documentation\/MapLibre\/MLNMapCamera\/cameraLookingAtCenterCoordinate:acrossDistance:pitch:heading:","interfaceLanguage":"occ"},"metadata